      "content": "That's a fair point about the distribution of benefits. But looking at it from the perspective of the people currently working in those \"traditional\" sectors, it's hard to see the \"economic boom\" as anything other than an existential threat. If the transition is going to be this disruptive, shouldn't we be focusing more on the reality that these policies represent a direct attack on the livelihoods of millions of working-class people? It feels like the \"green growth\" argument is just a way to hand-wave away the very real destruction of entire communities.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
